    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 all 14 tests pass, including the two new `Cp07Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when a client omits `registrationDate`, the server sets it to the current date, and the field is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` form (a supplied date is preserved).\n\nSince the DTOs are generated from the OpenAPI spec and persistence uses Spring Data JPA with `ddl-auto=none`, the change spans four layers:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string`, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Placing it there makes it accepted on the create request body and returned on the `Owner` response (which composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`). `format: date` generates a `LocalDate`, which serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD` \u2014 same mechanism already used by `Pet.birthDate`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a new `registration_date` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it in both directions by name.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after mapping the request, default `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when it's null. `updateOwner` is untouched, so an existing date is preserved on edits.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added `registration_date DATE` to the `owners` table in all four dialects (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`); hsqldb is the one the test suite actually runs against.\n\nVerification: `Cp07Tests` (defaults-to-today and keeps-supplied-date) pass, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS` at 14/14 with no regressions.",
